'' --diagnostics-file: one record per diagnostic, every kind, in the console's order.
''
'' The file is for an EDITOR -- docs/internals/diagnostics-file.md. What is asserted is
'' the contract, byte for byte where the bytes are the contract: the header, TAB between
'' fields, LF (never CRLF) after every record, the PHYSICAL line, a CHARACTER column, an
'' exclusive end, a note hung off the diagnostic before it as 'related', a TAB inside a
'' message turned into a space, and the 'end' record that says the run finished.
''
'' Paths are asserted by BASENAME: the file holds the absolute path, and that is this
'' checkout's path on this host.
''
'' The console is asserted too, because the file is written IN ADDITION to it: the
'' human rendering must not change shape because an editor asked for records.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --diagnostics-file build/.diagfile-records.tsv --dump-symbols tests/driver/src/diagfile-records.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: diagfile-records.bas(10,1): error TKO0309: #error: CONFIG not set
'' EXPECT-OUT: diagfile-records.bas(6,9): note: declared here
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-records.tsv :: tiko-diagnostics\t1\nwarning\tTKO0201\t
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-records.tsv :: diagfile-records.bas\t9\t19\t9\t24\tmissing closing quote in string literal\nnote\tTKO0315\t
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-records.tsv :: diagfile-records.bas\t5\t1\t5\t2\t#print "a b"\nerror\tTKO0309\t
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-records.tsv :: diagfile-records.bas\t10\t1\t10\t2\t#error: CONFIG not set\nerror\tTKO0603\t
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-records.tsv :: diagfile-records.bas\t7\t1\t7\t2\tcalling convention does not match the declaration of 'f'\nrelated\tTKO0901\t
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-records.tsv :: diagfile-records.bas\t6\t9\t6\t10\tdeclared here\nend\t2\t1\t1\n
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.diagfile-records.tsv :: \r
'' EXPECT-FILE-NOT-HAS: build/.diagfile-records.tsv :: a\tb
